#X obj 645 8 conv.dbfs2amp;
#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 161 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 The object converts a decibel full scale (dBFS) value
to a linear amplitude value. The conversion follows the formula amplitude
= 10^(dBFS / 20). A value of 0 dBFS corresponds to an amplitude of
1\. Positive dBFS values give amplitudes greater than 1 \, and negative
dBFS values give amplitudes between 0 and 1\.;
#X text 240 184 Note: dB values less than or equal to -144 are converted
to 0\.;
